            <ArticleTitle>HIV/AIDS and legal developments in Germany.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>79-83</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Case law has helped to define the legal environment for people infected and affected by HIV/AIDS in Germany. This article describes court decisions in three areas that may be of interest to Canadian readers: criminal law, confidentiality, and the use of illegal drugs to control pain. It also describes the situation of refugees with HIV/AIDS.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
